      "response": {
        "body": "Cancelling an HTTP/1 request after its final send could close the socket before its owner received cancellation, exposing native `:einval` or `:closed` instead of `:aborted`.\n\nNotify owners before closing tracked resources, including late registration and failure cleanup. At the post-send activation boundary, classify closed-handle errors as aborted only when cancellation is pending. Preserve native send failures already delivered before abort, independent transport errors, and parser failures.\n\nValidation: deterministic real TCP/OTP TLS regressions cover activation and final-send result publication, independent native errors, parser failure, peer closure, task join, and repeated original completion. Strict default/test compilation, full HTTP core/Fetch tests, formatting and Credo passed. ExSSL completion support remains outside this fix.\n\nFixes #122\n",
        "mergeCommit": {
          "oid": "9caf38cabdaa5fc1c65501632a28548ebd27d714"
        },
